# watchcat defaults for the R6800 build.
#
# The package default probes 8.8.8.8, which sits behind an international
# link on Chinese networks and produces false "no connectivity" reports
# (measured: intermittent failures and ~44 ms RTT, versus 15-19 ms for
# domestic resolvers).  A false positive here only creates log noise, but a
# genuine 6 h window would reboot the whole router.
#
# Two domestic, well-peered targets are used instead.  watchcat pings every
# host in the list and refreshes the failure timer as soon as ANY of them
# answers, so both would have to be unreachable for the reboot to trigger.
#
# period stays at the package default of 6 h: a shorter window would turn
# an upstream outage into a reboot loop, and a reboot cannot fix an upstream
# fault anyway.  223.5.5.5 is AliDNS, 180.76.76.76 is Baidu's resolver.

config watchcat
	option period '6h'
	option mode 'ping_reboot'
	option pinghosts '223.5.5.5 180.76.76.76'
	option pingperiod '60'
	option forcedelay '30'
